{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/queryingaworld"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most of the work in an entity component system is a loop over many similar entities: move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"everything that has a velocity, damage everything standing in fire, draw everything that has a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sprite. A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"query"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" describes which entities such a loop visits and which components it reads. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world answers a query with a lazy view of the matching entities, and an ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"update"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" uses the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"description to change components where they’re stored.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Read the entities that hold a set of components","anchor":"Read-the-entities-that-hold-a-set-of-components"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass component types to a world’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"query(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method to visit every entity that holds all of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them. Each row is a tuple of the entity, labeled ","type":"text"},{"code":"entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", followed by one component per type, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order you listed them:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Name(value: \"comet\"), Position(x: 1, y: 2), Velocity(dx: 3, dy: 4))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"rock\"), Position(x: 0, y: 0))","","for (_, name, position, velocity) in world.query(Name.self, Position.self, Velocity.self) {","    print(name.value, position.x + velocity.dx)","    \/\/ Prints \"comet 4.0\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rock has no velocity, so the query skips it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the entity is labeled, because a tuple’s labels can’t be named after its element types. To"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work with rows in a closure, such as when you sort or filter them, name the components by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destructuring the row rather than reaching for them by position:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Name(value: \"comet\"), Health(current: 3))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"moon\"), Health(current: 9))","","let strongest = world.query(Name.self, Health.self)","    .sorted { first, second in","        let (_, _, firstHealth) = first","        let (_, _, secondHealth) = second","        return firstHealth.current > secondHealth.current","    }","    .map { (_, name, _) in name.value }","print(strongest)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"moon\", \"comet\"]\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A view is a snapshot of the world at the moment you asked for it. Changing the world while you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterate the view doesn’t change the rows it shows, so you can despawn entities or insert"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components from inside the loop."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Narrow a query with a filter","anchor":"Narrow-a-query-with-a-filter"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some conditions matter without your needing to read the component. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"filter","type":"text"}]},{"text":" adds them:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryView\/with(_:)"},{"text":" requires types, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryView\/without(_:)"},{"text":" excludes them, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryView\/anyOf(_:)"},{"text":" requires an entity to pass at least one of several filters. The rows still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carry only the components you asked to read:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Name(value: \"comet\"), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"statue\"), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Frozen())","world.spawn(Name(value: \"rock\"))","","var moving: [String] = []","for (_, name) in world.query(Name.self).with(Velocity.self).without(Frozen.self) {","    moving.append(name.value)","}","print(moving)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"comet\"]\"","","let still = world.query(Name.self).anyOf(.with(Frozen.self), .without(Velocity.self))","print(still.count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryFilter","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value of its own, so you can build one once and apply it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryView\/filtered(by:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query\/filtered(by:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", or the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"where"},{"type":"text","text":" argument of an update."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To visit entities without reading any component, call ","type":"text"},{"code":"query()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no types and narrow the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityQueryView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" it returns:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Frozen())","world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","","for entity in world.query().with(Frozen.self) {","    world.remove(Frozen.self, from: entity)","}","print(world.query().with(Frozen.self).count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\""]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Describe a query once with a query value","anchor":"Describe-a-query-once-with-a-query-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"text":" holds a query’s terms and filter as a value that doesn’t belong to any world. Store it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compare it with another, and run it against any world:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let movers = Query(Position.self, Velocity.self).without(Frozen.self)","","var level = World()","level.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","level.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Frozen())","","var copy = level","copy.spawn(Position(x: 3, y: 3), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 1))","","print(level.query(movers).count, copy.query(movers).count)","\/\/ Prints \"1 2\""]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Match any of several components","anchor":"Match-any-of-several-components"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A query’s terms can include an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf"},{"type":"text","text":" group. An entity matches the group when it holds at least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one of its types, and the row holds a tuple with one optional per type, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" where the entity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lacks that type. The following example adds up the forces that push each entity, whichever of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wind and thrust it feels ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Wind"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thrust"},{"type":"text","text":" are components with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"force"},{"type":"text","text":" property):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Name(value: \"kite\"), Wind(force: 3))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"rocket\"), Thrust(force: 5), Wind(force: 1))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"rock\"))","","var forces: [String] = []","for (_, name, (wind, thrust)) in world.query(Query(Name.self, AnyOf<Wind, Thrust>.self)) {","    forces.append(\"\\(name.value): \\((wind?.force ?? 0) + (thrust?.force ?? 0))\")","}","print(forces)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"kite: 3.0\", \"rocket: 6.0\"]\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rock holds neither type, so the query skips it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Change components in place","anchor":"Change-components-in-place"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To change components while you visit them, use an update instead of a view. The method visits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entity that holds the component you change and the components you read. Its closure receives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the component to change as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" argument, and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryRow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" carrying the entity and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components it reads:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let comet = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","let statue = world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 1), Frozen())","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self, where: .without(Frozen.self)) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: comet])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\"","print(world[Position.self, of: statue])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 5.0, y: 5.0)\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An update can change up to three component types at once, and can take a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"type":"text","text":" in place of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the types it reads, which lets it read "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf"},{"type":"text","text":" groups:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let kite = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Wind(force: 2))","let rocket = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Thrust(force: 5))","","world.update(Position.self, over: Query(AnyOf<Wind, Thrust>.self)) { position, row in","    let (wind, thrust) = row.components","    position.x += (wind?.force ?? 0) + (thrust?.force ?? 0)","}","print(world[Position.self, of: kite].x, world[Position.self, of: rocket].x)","\/\/ Prints \"2.0 5.0\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An update can’t read a type it changes, and its closure can’t reach the world while it runs. To"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spawn, despawn or add components along the way, such as despawning the entities whose health runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, record the changes in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and apply them after the update."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Find what changed","anchor":"Find-what-changed"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The world stamps every component it adds or changes with its current "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/changeTick"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Filter on those stamps to visit only the entities whose components are new or changed:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query\/added(_:since:)"},{"type":"text","text":" passes the entities that gained a component after a tick, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query\/changed(_:since:)"},{"type":"text","text":" the ones whose component was added or changed after it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"hero\"), Health(current: 10))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"guard\"), Health(current: 8))","","let checkpoint = world.changeTick","world.advanceChangeTick()","world[Health.self, of: hero].current -= 3","","for (_, name, health) in world.query(Name.self, Health.self).changed(Health.self, since: checkpoint) {","    print(name.value, health.current)","    \/\/ Prints \"hero 7\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each filter checks every entity the visit would otherwise walk, so its cost grows with the number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of entities that hold the type, not with the number that changed. When few of many entities change"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between visits, log the type’s changes with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trackChanges(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"; the filters then start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the entities the log records after the tick:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","for _ in 0 ..< 1000 { world.spawn(Name(value: \"bystander\"), Health(current: 10)) }","let target = world.spawn(Name(value: \"target\"), Health(current: 10))","world.trackChanges(of: Health.self)","","let checkpoint = world.changeTick","world.advanceChangeTick()","world[Health.self, of: target].current -= 2","","for (_, name, health) in world.query(Name.self, Health.self).changed(Health.self, since: checkpoint) {","    print(name.value, health.current)","    \/\/ Prints \"target 8\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a tick, the filters compare against the world’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lastRun","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule sets it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the running system’s previous run, so in a system, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changed(Health.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" means “changed since"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this system last ran”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Filter in a system’s parameters","anchor":"Filter-in-a-systems-parameters"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A system receives a query as a parameter, already bound to the world it runs on, and iterates it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directly. Because a system’s parameters are types, it names its filter with filter types in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query\/Where"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/With"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Without"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Added"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Changed"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Allows"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf"},{"text":" of filter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types. For example, a system that visits the entities whose health changed since its previous","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run, and that aren’t frozen, takes a parameter of type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Query<Health>.Where<Changed<Health>, Without<Frozen>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and iterates it like a view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Speed up frequent queries","anchor":"Speed-up-frequent-queries"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A query of several types walks the storage of the type the fewest entities hold, and looks each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity up in the others. Three tools make frequent visits cheaper. None of them changes which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entities a query finds, only how it finds them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"group","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", made with ","type":"text"},{"code":"group(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", keeps a set of component types packed in the same order, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"query or update of exactly those types walks them side by side with no lookups. Group the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you visit together on every step:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let comet = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","world.group(Position.self, Velocity.self)","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","}","print(world[Position.self, of: comet].x)","\/\/ Prints \"1.0\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cached query"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", made with ","type":"text"},{"code":"cache(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", keeps a list of the entities that match a query’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"structure. A visit whose conditions imply the cache’s walks that list instead of a whole column.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Cache a query you run often that excludes most of the entities it would otherwise walk:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","for index in 0 ..< 10 {","    world.spawn(Position(x: Double(index), y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Asleep())","}","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let awake = Query(Position.self, Velocity.self).without(Asleep.self)","world.cache(awake)","print(world.query(awake).count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"value index"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", made with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", maps each value of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" component type to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entities holding it, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lookup(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" finds them without walking the type’s storage. Index a type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you look entities up by and whose values change rarely, such as a name:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ada = world.spawn(Name(value: \"ada\"), Health(current: 3))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"bob\"), Health(current: 4))","world.index(Name.self)","","print(world.lookup(Name(value: \"ada\")) == [ada])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To find entities by one property of a component rather than by the whole value, index the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property’s key path and look it up with ","type":"text"},{"code":"lookup(_:equals:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The component type doesn’t need to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", only the property:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Berth: Component { var dock: Int, number: Int }","","var world = World()","let ferry = world.spawn(Berth(dock: 2, number: 14))","world.spawn(Berth(dock: 3, number: 9))","world.index(\\Berth.number)","","print(world.lookup(\\Berth.number, equals: 14) == [ferry])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To find the entities whose property falls in a range, or to visit them in the order of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property, index the key path ordered with "},{"code":"index(ordered:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The property’s type needs to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"lookup(_:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes any range and returns the entities in the property’s order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"code":"entities(sortedBy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns every entity holding the component in that order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let fresh = world.spawn(Name(value: \"fresh\"), Health(current: 9))","let wounded = world.spawn(Name(value: \"wounded\"), Health(current: 2))","let dying = world.spawn(Name(value: \"dying\"), Health(current: 1))","world.index(ordered: \\Health.current)","","print(world.lookup(\\Health.current, in: ..<3) == [dying, wounded])","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","print(world.entities(sortedBy: \\Health.current) == [dying, wounded, fresh])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered index costs more to keep than an index by value, since each insert, removal and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"despawn finds the entity’s place in sorted order, so index a key path ordered only when you look"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it up by range or order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Querying-and-Updating-Entities","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryView","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityQueryView","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryRow","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryTerm","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntitiesView"],"title":"Querying and Updating Entities","generated":true}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Queryi